g  the cases column onto values  and similarly  the depths column onto values as well if  i close this  and let me squeeze it further  you can see we have our pivot table  ready  it has all the country names  and the total sum of the cases and the  total sum of debts that were reported in  each country  let's use this pivot table and  apply some shortcut keys  now first to group pivot table items  the shortcut key that i can use is  alt shift right arrow  so let's select a few  items from this pivot table i have  selected four  rows  and if i hit  alt shift right  arrow can see we have created a group it  says group 1 and it has  4 countries and the total cases as well  as the total number of debts  now  if you want to ungroup the pivot table  items you can use alt shift left arrow  so let me use alt shift left arrow  so first i have to select this group and  use alt shift left arrow  you can see we have ungrouped the pivot  table items  now if you want to hide a pivot table  item you can use control minus  so let's say i want to hide the values  for afghanistan i'll use control minus  to hide it  see afghanistan is no more there in this  pivot table  to unhide let me just use ctrl z it's  back  similarly  if you want to create a pivot chart  based on the pivot table on the same  sheet you can use alt f1  so let me hit alt f1  close this  and let me hit alt f1  there you go  we have our pivot chart  ready on the same sheet itself  so you can see there's a blue line and  there's orange line as well  the blue line represents the number of  cases and the orange line represents the  sum of deaths  this chart depicts that united states  has the highest number of cases as of  now  and then you can see we have  hungary iraq then there's portugal  and other countries as well  let me delete it  also if you want to create a pivot chart  on a new worksheet  the shortcut you can use is f11 so you  just have to hit  f11  so let me hit f11  you can see here  it has created a new 